@user "My own limited study on data science/ML has shown it’s all a black box which nobody can possibly unravel or begin to understand. It adjusts itself based on extremely complex math which makes it impossible to control"

Actually they can profile the neural nets to see which areas "light up", similar to a brain scan. And the math is actually not that complex- just a bunch of weights adjustments that settle upon a local minima through tons of repetition. 

The underlying "logic" may not be apparently, sure (it's more abstract patterns) but it's not quite the black box people make it out to be. The complexity of a neural net comes from the sheer combination of possibilities. Just 3 layers of 512 neurons comes out to 134,217,728 unique pathways.
